{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>YHWH will see.</b> He called the place thus, meaning: YHWH will see for the generations — that the merit of this binding (akedah) should stand for Israel in every generation. <b>As it is said to this day.</b> And also today, while I am on the mountain, YHWH will see my deeds before Him and requite me according to my righteousness. And so Abraham prayed for that hour and for the generations; thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory." "<b>And it appears</b> to me, to explain, the phrase <b>YHWH will see</b> refers to that hour; <b>as it is said to this day</b> — that is, what is destined to be said to this day — <b>on the mountain of YHWH it will be seen</b> for the generations, that is, it will be established. And it alludes to the midrash of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, that I cited above, that he prayed on the mountain and said: Master of the Universe, You swore and I swore, that I would not descend from the altar until I say something before You, etc. — when my children enter into trouble, remember this for them. And therefore it appears that the 'saying' here is prayer. And because this place was called by the hand of Abraham יראה, and by the hand of Shem, son of Noah, it was called שלם, therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, called it ירושלם — a name joined from two righteous ones of the world." "<b>And they said</b> in the Midrash that Isaac saw the form of a lion upon the altar. And the meaning of the lion is the fear of Isaac (פחד יצחק); and perhaps it is the Lion of the supernal house (אריא דבי עלאה) that our Rabbis, of blessed memory, mentioned in tractate Ḥullin. And behold, it is hinted at in this verse, for it says ״בהר ה׳ יראה״ — on the mountain of YHWH it will be seen — for the form of a lion was seen to him on the mountain of YHWH." "<b>And in Bereshit Rabbah:</b> ״ה׳ יראה״ — He showed him the Temple (בית המקדש) built and destroyed and built. Built, as it says ״ה׳ יראה״, and it is written (Deuteronomy 16:16) ״יראה כל זכורך״. Destroyed: ״אשר יאמר היום בהר ה׳״ — as it says (Lamentations 5:18) ״על הר ציון ששמם״. It will be seen — and behold it is built, as it says (Psalms 102) ״כי בנה ה׳ ציון נראה בכבודו״. Thus far."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {2 "פחד יצחק ('fear of Isaac') is itself a divine epithet from Genesis 31:42, here linked to the imagery of the lion; both senses carried simultaneously in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:17.665871516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}